WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.921 --> 00:00:08.216
Skylar Mays: I always tap his locker, just like it was in high school.

00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:12.721
It hits me every time.

00:00:17.225 --> 00:00:19.269
Fay Sims: Him and Wayde laced up next to each other.

00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:22.230
Their lockers were side by side for years.

00:00:22.605 --> 00:00:26.192
Skylar mentioned that everything to him feels different.

00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:28.653
It’s—it just feels different.

00:00:31.573 --> 00:00:33.283
Wayde was the only child.

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:38.121
He just always had a big heart, even as a child

00:00:39.497 --> 00:00:41.750
He never wanted you mad at him.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:45.503
You know, he was just a bundle of joy

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:51.009
I just noticed how much everyone gravitated toward

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:54.971
him because he was just so friendly to everybody.

00:00:54.971 --> 00:00:57.599
He made everybody feel like they were special.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.809
Once we were able to get on the same AAU team.

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:01.811
That's when I first started to hang around him.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:04.272
I just knew that was somebody that I wanted to be like

00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:06.316
and somebody I wanted to be around as much as possible.

00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:10.945
All right, Skylar Mays here with small forward/power forward/center

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.990
Gatorade Player of the Year, Wayde Sims.

00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:15.116
- How you doin’, guys?

00:01:15.658 --> 00:01:20.330
- All right, you know, I like to get kinda personal in my interviews

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.499
so I wanna ask you, how's Leslie doin’?

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:24.042
Leslie Slaughter, your girlfriend.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.669
- Oh, that's my girlfriend, that's my girl.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.297
You know, we doin’ pretty good.

00:01:29.506 --> 00:01:30.173
That's it.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:32.592
- You guys had, like, a good chemistry.

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.052
You guys joked around a lot with each other.

00:01:34.052 --> 00:01:35.720
You guys balanced each other out a little bit.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.889
Describe your relationship with him.

00:01:38.223 --> 00:01:40.600
- Yeah, I like to say it's kind of a yin and yang.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.103
I'm more of a, you know, steady guy, and

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:46.815
he's just the flamboyant person who does a lot of

00:01:46.815 --> 00:01:49.692
theatrics that everybody, you know, loves, and

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.362
he keeps everybody easygoing.

00:01:52.362 --> 00:01:54.906
So I think that was really beneficial for me

00:01:54.906 --> 00:01:58.326
and helped me be myself but also open up.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.287
- Wayde took Skylar’s brothers and sisters

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:04.332
as his siblings, and they accepted

00:02:04.332 --> 00:02:06.042
Wayde, like, as their brother.

00:02:10.171 --> 00:02:12.799
- We got to a point where I coached him 

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:15.260
and then I had to turn him over to somebody else, and

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.220
just to see him grow, we were all happy and excited.

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:22.767
Fay: I think he always knew that he was—I think he was just tryin’ to play me.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:27.689
I secretly prayed that he would stay here and go to LSU. 

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:31.651
I remember one day he just kinda entertained maybe going

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.444
somewhere off, and I was

00:02:33.444 --> 00:02:35.738
like, “Oh god, no, please.”

00:02:35.738 --> 00:02:36.948
- And I’m excited to be playin’

00:02:36.948 --> 00:02:38.199
basketball at LSU next year.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.830
Wayne: It was exciting to me, bein’ a dad and a former player. 

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:47.584
It's always an honor to see your kid go in your footsteps.

00:02:47.792 --> 00:02:49.586
- Did Wayde's commitment here affect yours?

00:02:49.711 --> 00:02:52.839
- Absolutely, absolutely. I loved playin’ with Wayde.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.883
We knew each other’s game in and out.

00:02:54.924 --> 00:02:58.303
You know, we played with each other for 10, 12-plus years. 

00:02:58.803 --> 00:03:00.722
So, wanted to keep it goin’.

00:03:02.974 --> 00:03:05.685
- How did the bond between you guys evolve

00:03:06.102 --> 00:03:08.146
once you got to college, once you got to LSU?

00:03:09.606 --> 00:03:13.943
- Um...definitely grew stronger. I think we—the more we

00:03:13.943 --> 00:03:15.612
were around each other, our, just, relationship

00:03:15.612 --> 00:03:16.654
just grew every day.

00:03:16.821 --> 00:03:19.199
Mays: When Coach would get on us pretty bad, he was the one

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:20.700
who would kinda ease everything up.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.286
I think he was a glue guy in the way he played because

00:03:23.286 --> 00:03:25.246
he played to make other guys better.

00:03:25.246 --> 00:03:26.247
He played to win.

00:03:26.789 --> 00:03:27.832
You know, anybody likes to play with

00:03:27.832 --> 00:03:29.876
somebody like that, so.

00:03:31.586 --> 00:03:33.129
It was so effortless for him to

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:35.840
help this team win games.

00:03:40.678 --> 00:03:42.347
- Members of the LSU basketball

00:03:42.347 --> 00:03:43.598
team are grieving tonight.

00:03:43.598 --> 00:03:45.308
- Cellphone video shows the moments

00:03:45.308 --> 00:03:46.768
before Wayde Sims was shot.

00:03:50.355 --> 00:03:52.273
- I got the phone call in the middle of the

00:03:52.273 --> 00:03:55.568
night, and I just remember us racing to the hospital

00:03:55.818 --> 00:03:59.530
and, um...and then it—I don't know.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:01.491
I really don't remember, like, a whole lot.

00:04:01.491 --> 00:04:05.411
I actually don't remember all of the month of October or November.

00:04:11.042 --> 00:04:12.460
- I was sleeping.

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.462
It was pretty early.

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:20.051
Obviously that woke me up and, I

00:04:20.051 --> 00:04:22.220
mean, that day was for the most part a blur.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.097
- I was just prayin’ to God that he would

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:27.600
be all right. Um, you know, that—

00:04:27.684 --> 00:04:29.978
I know he was shot. You know, just

00:04:29.978 --> 00:04:32.272
I would hope that, you know, he would survive.

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:33.773
We got there or whatever, but, you

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:35.191
know, unfortunately wasn’t—

00:04:39.696 --> 00:04:41.364
- We begin with the tragedy hitting

00:04:41.364 --> 00:04:42.448
the Baton Rouge sports world.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:43.866
LSU basketball star Wayde

00:04:43.866 --> 00:04:45.660
Sims, shot and killed overnight.

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:54.711
- I just paused for a minute and just

00:04:54.711 --> 00:04:58.673
kinda sat back; like, I was in shock and disbelief.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:04.595
And I just couldn't stop crying.

00:05:04.595 --> 00:05:05.763
I didn't know what to do.

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:07.181
I called my parents because my parents

00:05:07.265 --> 00:05:11.352
are obviously close with Wayde like his

00:05:11.352 --> 00:05:13.563
are with me, and, um...

00:05:15.398 --> 00:05:17.015
And just cried.

00:05:21.237 --> 00:05:22.518
- I feel like everyone who

00:05:22.518 --> 00:05:27.115
knew Wayde...I mean—

00:05:32.581 --> 00:05:35.439
Everyone who knew Wayde knew

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:38.151
that he just smiled all the time.

00:05:38.175 --> 00:05:40.760
Just a loving person, and

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:42.231
his smile was contagious

00:05:42.921 --> 00:05:45.717
For me, it kinda feels like he’s just on

00:05:45.717 --> 00:05:49.053
a really long vacation and he forgot his phone here.

00:05:51.867 --> 00:05:53.970
It's just, it's just really hard for me.

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:56.464
It's hard for all of us.

00:05:56.464 --> 00:06:01.990
- My heart breaks for Skylar. I mean, it just, it just breaks for Skylar.

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:05.813
He checks on me, and I'll check on him, and

00:06:05.813 --> 00:06:07.638
we’ll just try to, you know, keep in touch. 

00:06:07.638 --> 00:06:13.898
But, you know, I feel like I'm dying in the inside but, you

00:06:13.898 --> 00:06:17.962
know, I just—my heart just aches for him as well.

00:06:19.479 --> 00:06:21.086
Fay: It’s your worst nightmare.

00:06:21.522 --> 00:06:23.989
So I always say that the worst thing that could have

00:06:23.989 --> 00:06:25.986
ever happened to me has happened.

00:06:27.556 --> 00:06:30.606
Wayde was my entire life.

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:37.484
How do you feel his presence as a team?

00:06:38.054 --> 00:06:41.104
Yeah, sometimes when some shots go in in the

00:06:41.104 --> 00:06:43.207
game, I’m like, “Yeah, that was Wayde.”

00:06:46.557 --> 00:06:49.964
Fay: I don't feel that I could ever fill the void.

00:06:49.964 --> 00:06:52.300
I just don't foresee that happening.

00:06:52.893 --> 00:06:56.528
I know that I'll be empty, I

00:06:56.528 --> 00:06:58.537
say for the rest of my life.

00:06:59.499 --> 00:07:03.340
My heart has a hole, and I tell him it bleeds every day.

00:07:04.887 --> 00:07:06.802
I don't ever see that being repaired.

00:07:06.802 --> 00:07:09.521
I know by the grace of God, He could

00:07:09.521 --> 00:07:13.060
change, you know, situations, but I

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:15.238
just—right now I can't see that.

